# Chaos: cheaper creature icon count text and no colour list copy per draw (O217; client/BASE.md "0137"; src/client/creature.h/.cpp,
# src/framework/graphics/cachedtext.h/.cpp, drawqueue.h/.cpp; after 0001-0136).
# Finishes the per-frame text work of 0133. The count drawn next to a creature icon went through DrawQueue::addText (hash of the
# string, mutex, map search, again on the graphics thread) and g_fonts.getFont("verdana-cap-bold") (a name search) once per icon
# per frame: now the font is found once per creature and each of the (at most 4) icons owns a chaos::TextSlot, keyed like
# CachedText's (font id, font texture, box, alignment) with the count itself as the revision (the text is its decimal form).
# DrawQueueItemTextEntryColored copied the colour vector of the speech on every draw: CachedText now keeps one immutable
# shared copy (dropped by update(), the only way the list changes) and the item holds a shared_ptr to it. Same entries, same
# TextRender::drawEntry / drawColoredEntry, same painter calls: the picture is the same. The edge-clipped name box (a size change
# that rebuilds its layout) is left as it is. Not built or run.
diff --git a/src/client/creature.cpp b/src/client/creature.cpp
